The other six primary sources the page cites.

Bitsight's ToolShell threat brief and Fastly's analysis of the remote code execution are the two the page also links from its header. Censys's advisory of July 21 carries exposure data. Logpoint describes SharePoint becoming a gateway to remote code execution. The MITRE page defines T1606, Forge Web Credentials, one of the two techniques the page maps to stage 04. BleepingComputer reports the Energy Department confirming the impact on its systems.

The background slides name their own sources: OWASP, MITRE ATT&CK and Microsoft Learn.

